A hand-built solid RAR5 archive whose dictionary size changes between
entries.  Each entry is one compressed block that uses fixed Huffman
tables (9-bit literal/length codes, 6-bit distance slots).

  first.bin:  128 KiB dictionary, not solid.  The 17 literals
              "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQ" followed by matches at distance 17,
              for a total of 200000 bytes of that repeating pattern.
  grow.bin:   256 KiB dictionary, solid.  One match of length 17 at
              distance 10: "CDEFGHIJKLCDEFGHI".
  shrink.bin: 128 KiB dictionary, solid.  One match of length 17 at
              distance 31, reaching back into first.bin and through
              grow.bin: "PQABCDEFGHIJKLCDE".

All entries carry CRC32s.  Both matches read history that was written
more than 128 KiB into the stream, which is stored at a different
window position after the dictionary size changes.

